From 2d2d617db428961aad36438d5397ac30db90080c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1aeo <github@1aeo.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 07:03:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] metrics: Count onion service descriptor uploads by
 outcome

An HSDir answers every rejected descriptor upload with the same 400
"Invalid HS descriptor. Rejected.", whether the descriptor didn't parse
or validate, or it was valid but not newer than the one in our cache,
which happens without any fault when several instances publish for the
same onion address. Uploads refused because they don't come over an
anonymous circuit aren't counted anywhere either.

Add tor_relay_hsdir_post_total{action=...} to the MetricsPort with the
"success", "bad_url", "invalid", "not_newer" and "single_hop" actions,
in the same way as tor_relay_intro1_total. To tell "invalid" from
"not_newer", make hs_cache_store_as_dir() return -2 when the descriptor
is valid but not newer. Its only caller checks for a negative value.

All the counting is in dircache.c, which is only built with the relay
module, so no stub is needed when it is disabled.
